Provenance
----------
Produces espeak compatible phoneme codes, made from the ground up: the same Kokoro/misaki-style codes
Leokani-tts and Kokoro use. It contains no espeak-ng code or data files.

Third-party credits
-------------------
- GeoNames (geonames.org), CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/): place names in the
  lexicon's word list.
- Kokoro-82M by hexgrad (https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M), Apache-2.0: the phoneme set the output is
  written in.
- misaki by hexgrad (https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki), Apache-2.0: the phoneme codes (misaki's set, which
  Kokoro uses), and words from its us_gold and us_silver lexicons in the lexicon's word list (their
  pronunciations are not used).
- The CMU Pronouncing Dictionary (https://github.com/cmusphinx/cmudict), BSD-2-Clause: words in the lexicon's
  word list (its pronunciations are not used). Its notice follows.

